From: lane <lane@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 05:06:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] fix(typed-generator): re-freeze the
 blur173..scanline177 milestone chain

Same class as every other milestone-chain fix this session: the 0ed489ec
corpus bump's unexcluded programs (filter/adjust, filter/chrome:chMap,
filter/grade:primary/vignette, filter/invert:inv, filter/text:text,
filter/tint:colorize, mixer/alphaMask, mixer/blendMode,
synth/media:mediaInput -- 8 of the 10 non-grade ones ride in here
unexcluded; grade:primary/vignette are excluded by this chain's own set)
ride into every one of these four adjacent reconstructions, and the
post-integ4-merge MRT/julia/texture-driver emitter changes move them
again on top of that.

Important correction caught by cross-checking rather than trusted by
label: this chain's "scanline177" is NOT the same program-set
composition as test_glyph_map_nonnegative_int_shift.py's/
test_emboss_color_style.py's "scanline177"/"glyph178" milestones despite
the identical name -- this chain's own exclusion set additionally
excludes filter/grime:grime and 8 more early-landing programs that the
edge/glyph-map/emboss chain does not, so it lands on a different actual
196-... program composition at the same nominal count. Recomputing this
chain's own four states directly (via each test's own literal exclusion
set, never reusing a same-named state from a different test file) is
what caught this before it became a wrong re-freeze; a first attempt
reusing the wrong "scanline177" value produced completely different
hashes, exposing the mismatch immediately.

Re-pinned all four tests' current+prior artifact hashes (typed_slice.cpp
+ typed_manifest.json; catalog.hpp was already correct throughout,
confirmed unchanged). All four pass together (Ran 4 tests ... OK).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EU6jaFnvpzrcsgg8pXrwK2
